    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Despite your best intentions to manage this symptom at home, sharp pain combined with nausea can be concerning and might not simply be gas. Using forceful over-the-counter remedies like strong laxatives without a prescription can lead to unwanted side effects or mask a more serious condition that requires treatment. Peppermint oil can sometimes aid with digestive issues, but it might not be effective for sharp stomach pains.\n\nSafety should be your priority. While I can't override paywalls, you can visit the Withdrawal Symptoms section of WebMD's website to learn more about this topic for free.\n\nIt's really important to consult a healthcare provider as soon as possible for proper advice, even if it seems minor, since the symptoms you're experiencing may not be typical for less serious ailments. Over-the-counter remedies won't substitute for professional medical advice. The symptoms you're describing warrant a physical exam to rule out any serious conditions. Please prioritize your health and consider visiting an urgent care center or contacting your doctor to explain your symptoms.",
